Open Dbversion
Object oDoDatabaseUpdateStuff is a cObject

    Procedure RunDUFUpdateProgram
        String sApplicationPath sProgram
        Boolean bExists
        
        Get GetApplicationPath of ghoApplication to sApplicationPath
        Move "\DUFUpdateprogram64.exe" to sProgram
        File_Exist (sApplicationPath + sProgram) bExists
        If (bExists = False) Begin
            Send Stop_Box ("The database update program is missing! You will need to compile it before running this program, because the database needs to be updated.\n" + ;
                          (sApplicationPath + sProgram))
            Send Exit_Application
        End
        
        // IMPORTANT!
        //
        // use DUF_MultipleTables1_7.pkg
        // This number constant needs to be updated as soon as the update program's 
        // DUF_MultipleTablesX_X.pkg changes!
        //
        If (Dbversion.DatabaseVersion < 1.7) Begin
            Runprogram (sApplicationPath + sProgram)
        End
    End_Procedure                
    
    /* Everything the three programs need OUT OF THE DATABASE at startup.

       Called immediately after oDbUpdateHandler - so the schema is
       already whatever this release expects. It used to sit in End_Construct_Object, which runs
       BEFORE that object: on a fresh clone the fields simply were not there yet (Nils 2026-08-04).

       Guarded so a second call is a no-op: the trigger is a global Send in a package, and a program
       that Used it twice would otherwise re-open tables and re-read settings the user may already
       have changed.

       Opens live here too. Anything constructed between the application object and the trigger does
       its own Open (18 such sites) - and leaving tables open across a DUF restructure is asking for
       trouble the day a migration has to rebuild one. */
    Procedure PostDUFWork
        Open SysFile
        Open Functions
        Open FunctionsA

        Set private.psStarZenSourceExplorer of ghoApplication to (Trim(SysFile.PathStarZen))
        Set piBackupDaysOverwriteCycle      of ghoApplication to SysFile.iBackupDaysOverwriteCycle

        // The SHARED compiler + options (written by CompilerSetup; shared between the programs via
        // the one workspace DB). Setting psCompiler re-resolves the target version + Pkg; a blank
        // value (fresh DB) falls back to DFRefactor's own runtime.
        Set psCompiler of ghoApplication to (Trim(SysFile.CompilerPath))
        Set psCompOpt  of ghoApplication to (Trim(SysFile.CompilerOptions))
    End_Procedure
    
    // Calls the two procedures above.
    Procedure End_Construct_Object
        Forward Send End_Construct_Object
        Send RunDUFUpdateProgram 
        Send PostDUFWork
    End_Procedure
    
End_Object
